shaderc: GLSL ES shaders that use the bit encoders stay GLSL ES 3.00

A fragment shader that calls floatBitsToUint, floatBitsToInt, intBitsToFloat or uintBitsToFloat raised its GLSL ES
version to 3.10, as images and storage buffers do. The bit encoders are GLSL ES 3.00 built-ins, and at 3.10 SPIRV-Cross
writes code only 3.10 compiles, such as mix() of integer vectors for a select between two ivec2: OpenGL ES 3.0 and
WebGL 2 reject the shader. The bit encoders now raise only the desktop GLSL version.

diff --git a/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp b/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
index 8b7dc2da0..3f9d279a9 100644
--- a/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
+++ b/tools/shaderc/shaderc.cpp
@@ -2339,8 +2339,12 @@ namespace bgfx
 								&& !bx::findIdentifierMatch(preprocessedInput, s_bitsToEncoders).isEmpty()
 								;
 
-							if (!bx::strFind(preprocessedInput, "layout(std430").isEmpty()
-							||  !bx::strFind(preprocessedInput, "image2D").isEmpty()
+							const bool usesImagesOrStorageBuffers = false
+								|| !bx::strFind(preprocessedInput, "layout(std430").isEmpty()
+								|| !bx::strFind(preprocessedInput, "image2D").isEmpty()
+								;
+
+							if (usesImagesOrStorageBuffers
 							||  usesBitsToEncoders)
 							{
 								if (glsl_profile < 430)
@@ -2348,8 +2352,11 @@ namespace bgfx
 									glsl_profile = 430;
 								}
 
-								// Images, and storage buffers, require ESSL 3.10.
-								if (0 != esslVersion)
+								// Images, and storage buffers, require ESSL 3.10. The bit encoders are ESSL 3.00
+								// built-ins: raised for them, SPIRV-Cross writes ESSL 3.10 code (mix() of integer
+								// vectors) that OpenGL ES 3.0 and WebGL 2 reject.
+								if (0 != esslVersion
+								&&  usesImagesOrStorageBuffers)
 								{
 									esslVersion = bx::max<uint32_t>(esslVersion, 310);
 								}
